  "RN7SL3": "The signal recognition particle (SRP) is a cytoplasmic ribonucleoprotein complex that mediates cotranslational insertion of secretory proteins into the lumen of the endoplasmic reticulum. The SRP consists of 6 polypeptides (e.g., SRP19; MIM 182175) and a 7SL RNA molecule, such as RN7SL3, that is partially homologous to Alu DNA (Ullu and Weiner, 1984 [PubMed 6084597]).[supplied by OMIM, Jul 2008].",
