  "MTERF4": "Enables rRNA binding activity. Predicted to be involved in rRNA processing and regulation of transcription, DNA-templated. Predicted to act upstream of or within several processes, including mitochondrial transcription; protein targeting to mitochondrion; and ribosome assembly. Located in cytosol and mitochondrion. Part of mitochondrial large ribosomal subunit. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]",
